# AYC Build Protocol

## Drive constraint (non-negotiable)

- **All project files live on `H:\AYC` only.**
- **Never create, install, cache, download, build, or write any file type to `C:\`.**
- C: is full. Treat any path under `C:\` as forbidden for this project.
- Configure tools so outputs stay on H: (workspace, `node_modules`, build artifacts, caches, temp, logs, env files, git objects for this repo).
- If a tool defaults to C: (npm cache, temp, user profile, AppData), redirect it to H: or refuse and ask how to redirect — do not write to C:.

## GitHub → Netlify continuous deploy (required)

- Remote: https://github.com/Grappe501/ayc · branch `main` · workspace `H:\AYC`
- **After every major update / completed slice / substantial pass:** automatically `git add`, `commit`, and `git push -u origin HEAD` (or `origin main`) so Netlify can deploy.
- Do **not** wait for the user to ask for commit/push during normal build work — this protocol authorizes it.
- Commit messages describe the delivered capability (conventional style: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, etc.).
- Never commit secrets, `.env`, personal exports, API keys, or real youth contact data.
- Never force-push to `main` unless Steve explicitly requests it.
- Never skip hooks unless Steve explicitly requests it.
- If validation is required for the slice, prefer committing only after `npm run validate` succeeds (docs-only updates may commit without full app validate).
- After push, note that Netlify will pick up `main` once the site is linked to this repo.

## Master build plan intake

- The full website is defined by a **master build plan** delivered as markdown files.
- Place every plan markdown under `H:\AYC\docs\master-build-plan\` (and subfolders if needed).
- When the user provides markdown: **save it into that tree**, keep filenames clear, do not leave plan content only in chat.
- While ingesting: **read and understand** what is being built. Update `00-UNDERSTANDING.md` as plan docs arrive.
- Do **not** start full site implementation until the user says the master build plan is finished **and** Volume VIII (or explicit authorization) is in place.

## Canonical mission

Use the locked mission in `docs/master-build-plan/02-AYC-VISION-CANONICAL.md` verbatim on the landing page. Do not rewrite.

## Governing docs

Read Volumes I–VII before implementing. Follow Volume VII gates, slice naming, build-return format, and stop conditions. Stay inside the approved slice. Do not invent screens or expand the roadmap. Keep secrets out of code and chat output.

Repo: [Grappe501/ayc](https://github.com/Grappe501/ayc) · Workspace: `H:\AYC`. No casual runtime imports from other SOSWebsite projects.

## Implementation gate

- Do **not** start application implementation until **Volume VIII (Phase 1 Master Implementation Plan)** is ingested, **unless** Steve explicitly authorizes an earlier start.
- Volume VI is the exact Phase 1 UI contract — **do not invent** unapproved screens, actions, fields, or navigation.
- After Vol VIII (or explicit authorization): follow Phase 0 then Phase 1 slice sequence; build only on `H:\AYC`.

## After the plan is complete

- Confirm all plan markdown is on H: under `docs/master-build-plan/`.
- Build Phase 1 from Volumes I–VIII into `H:\AYC` (still never on C:).
- Prefer governing volumes over assumptions. Report BUILD RETURN after every slice.
- Commit and push each major slice automatically per this protocol.

## Working style

- Prefer absolute paths on `H:\AYC\...`.
- Keep plan markdown as source of truth until build starts; do not invent major scope outside the plan.
